IMPORT prelude

-- Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- the rates of income tax on an individual (s 3 "tax-free threshold",
-- "prescribed non-resident", "resident taxpayer", "ordinary taxable income"; s 12(1); Schedule 7 Part I clauses 1 and 4, Part II
-- clauses 1 and 4, Part III), the part-year residency period (ss 16, 18, 20(1)), and the rates on a company (s 23(2), (6);
-- s 23AA "base rate entity").
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 66, compilation date 1 July 2026, includes amendments up to Act No. 50, 2026 (Register id
-- C2026C00300), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03348.txt. The deposit drops every formula that was set as
-- an image ("in accordance with the following formula:" is followed by nothing), including s 20's pro-rating formula and
-- Schedule 7 clauses 2 and 3.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0019 in ../../../requirements.jsonl (priority 1), raised 3 times by the Western Australian
-- cradle-to-grave scenarios: chloe c045 (2024-10-20, first tax return for 2023-24, taxable income $27,500), chloe c048
-- (2025-10-25, second return for 2024-25, taxable income $71,500) and daniel d04a (2033-11-30, Jarrah Legal Technologies Pty
-- Ltd's first company return: "What rate"). SCOPED to the provisions the lives cite (Schedule 7; s 23 base rate entity), with
-- the definitions, residency tests, the superannuation and employment-termination remainders and the working holiday maker
-- rules that change the Schedule 7 answer.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: Schedule 7 clauses 2 and 3 (abnormal income averaging; formula not in the deposit); the pro-rating formula in
-- s 20 (not in the deposit -- the pro-rated threshold is an INPUT); ss 12(4)-(13), 12AA, 12A, 13-15 (trustees, primary
-- producers, minors' income under Div 6AA); Schedules 8 to 12; s 23(3)-(5), (7), 23A and ss 25-30 (RSA providers, PDFs, credit
-- unions, life insurers, trusts, super funds, sovereign entities); s 23AB's list of passive income (base rate entity passive
-- income is an INPUT). Tax offsets (the low income tax offset), the Medicare levy and HELP repayments are other Acts.
--
-- A year of income is named by the calendar year in which it begins: 2024 is the 2024-25 year of income.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT FOR PUBLIC USE. See NOTES.md.

§ `Income Tax Rates Act 1986 -- rates`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER, `from` IS A NUMBER, `width` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the slice` MEANS
    IF `amount` AT MOST `from` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `amount` MINUS `from` GREATER THAN `width` THEN `width` ELSE `amount` MINUS `from`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- A width large enough to stand for "exceeds $190,000" with no upper limit.
`no upper limit` MEANS 1000000000000

§§ `s 3 -- the tax-free threshold`

-- s 3(1): "tax-free threshold means $18,200."
`the tax-free threshold` MEANS 18200

§§ `s 3 -- prescribed non-resident, resident taxpayer`

-- s 3(1): "prescribed non-resident ... means a person who, at all times during the year of income, is a non-resident, not being
-- a person to whom, at any time during the year of income, compensation or a pension, allowance or benefit is payable under:
-- (a) the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986; ... (ba) the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004; or (c) the Social
-- Security Act 1991; being compensation or a pension, allowance or benefit in respect of which the person is liable to be
-- assessed and to pay income tax in Australia."
-- "resident taxpayer ... means a taxpayer who is not a prescribed non-resident".

DECLARE Individual HAS
    `year of income begins` IS A NUMBER
    `a non-resident at all times during the year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid an assessable veterans', military compensation or social security payment in the year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `became or ceased to be a resident during the year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an eligible pensioner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `pro-rated tax-free threshold` IS A NUMBER
    `taxable income` IS A NUMBER
    `superannuation remainder` IS A NUMBER
    `employment termination remainder` IS A NUMBER
    `working holiday taxable income` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `p` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a prescribed non-resident` MEANS
        `p`'s `a non-resident at all times during the year`
    AND (NOT `p`'s `paid an assessable veterans', military compensation or social security payment in the year`)

GIVEN `p` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a resident taxpayer` MEANS NOT `a prescribed non-resident` `p`

§§ `ss 16, 18, 20(1) -- part-year residency and the pro-rated threshold`

-- s 18(1): part-year residency periods arise where the person "commenced to be a resident" or "ceased to be a resident" during
-- a month of the year of income. s 18(2): a period is not one "if (a) the person is an eligible pensioner in relation to the
-- year of income; or (b) the period is the whole of the year of income."
-- s 20(1): the Schedule 7 Part I reference to the tax-free threshold is read "as if [it] were a reference to the amount
-- calculated in accordance with the following formula" -- THE FORMULA IS NOT IN THE DEPOSIT. The pro-rated threshold is an
-- INPUT here.
GIVEN `p` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`there is a part-year residency period` MEANS
        `p`'s `became or ceased to be a resident during the year`
    AND (NOT `p`'s `an eligible pensioner`)

GIVEN `p` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the threshold that applies` MEANS
    IF `there is a part-year residency period` `p` THEN `p`'s `pro-rated tax-free threshold`
    ELSE `the tax-free threshold`

§§ `s 3 -- ordinary taxable income`

-- s 3(1): "ordinary taxable income means the taxable income, reduced by the superannuation remainder of the taxable income and
-- by the employment termination remainder of the taxable income." (The remainders are the parts included under a maximum tax
-- rate provision in Divisions 301 and 82 of the 1997 Act that do not give rise to a tax offset: INPUTS here.)
GIVEN `p` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the ordinary taxable income` MEANS
    `p`'s `taxable income` MINUS `p`'s `superannuation remainder` MINUS `p`'s `employment termination remainder`

§§ `Schedule 7 Part I -- resident taxpayers`

-- Clause 1: "(a) 45% for the superannuation remainder (if any) of the taxable income; (aa) 45% for the employment termination
-- remainder (if any) of the taxable income; (b) for each part of the ordinary taxable income specified in the table applicable to
-- the year of income -- the rate applicable under that table."
-- Three tables only: "for the 2024-25 or 2025-26 year of income" (item 1: "exceeds the tax-free threshold but does not exceed
-- $45,000" -- 16%); "for the 2026-27 year of income" (15%); "for the 2027-28 year of income or a later year of income" (14%).
-- Items 2 to 4 are the same in all three: over $45,000 to $135,000 -- 30%; over $135,000 to $190,000 -- 37%; over $190,000 -- 45%.
-- THERE IS NO TABLE FOR 2023-24 OR EARLIER IN THIS COMPILATION.
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the item 1 rate in percent` MEANS
    IF `year` LESS THAN 2024 THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `year` AT MOST 2025 THEN JUST 16
        ELSE IF `year` EQUALS 2026 THEN JUST 15
            ELSE JUST 14

GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the deposit has a resident table for the year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the item 1 rate in percent` `year`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST `r` THEN TRUE

-- The tax under a resident table on the parts of ordinary taxable income from $0 up to `upto`.
GIVEN `threshold` IS A NUMBER, `item 1 rate` IS A NUMBER, `upto` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the resident table tax up to` MEANS
        `the slice` `upto` `threshold` (45000 MINUS `threshold`) TIMES `item 1 rate` DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `upto` 45000 90000 TIMES 30 DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `upto` 135000 55000 TIMES 37 DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `upto` 190000 `no upper limit` TIMES 45 DIVIDED BY 100

-- Convenience: a resident with no remainders, no working holiday income and the full threshold.
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER, `income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the resident tax on ordinary taxable income` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the item 1 rate in percent` `year`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `r` THEN JUST (`the resident table tax up to` `the tax-free threshold` `r` `income`)

§§ `Schedule 7 Part II -- non-resident taxpayers`

-- One table, "for the 2024-25 year of income or a later year of income": up to $135,000 -- "The second resident personal tax
-- rate"; over $135,000 to $190,000 -- "The third resident personal tax rate"; over $190,000 -- 45%. s 3: the second and third
-- resident personal tax rates are items 2 and 3 of the Part I table for the year -- 30% and 37% in every deposited table.
-- No tax-free threshold.
GIVEN `upto` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the non-resident table tax up to` MEANS
        `the slice` `upto` 0 135000 TIMES 30 DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `upto` 135000 55000 TIMES 37 DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `upto` 190000 `no upper limit` TIMES 45 DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `Schedule 7 Part III -- working holiday makers`

-- "Tax rates for working holiday makers for the 2024-25 year of income or a later year of income": up to $45,000 -- 15%; over
-- $45,000 to $135,000 -- 30%; over $135,000 to $190,000 -- 37%; over $190,000 -- 45%. (s 3A: a working holiday maker holds a
-- Subclass 417 or 462 visa, a qualifying bridging visa or a COVID-19 pandemic event 408 visa.)
GIVEN `upto` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the working holiday table tax up to` MEANS
        `the slice` `upto` 0 45000 TIMES 15 DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `upto` 45000 90000 TIMES 30 DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `upto` 135000 55000 TIMES 37 DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `upto` 190000 `no upper limit` TIMES 45 DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `Schedule 7 Parts I and II clause 4 -- putting it together`

-- Clause 4 (Parts I and II alike): "(a) count the taxpayer's working holiday taxable income ... as the first parts (starting
-- from $0) of the taxpayer's ordinary taxable income for the purposes of the table in clause 1 ...; and (b) do not apply the
-- rates in that table to that working holiday taxable income". So the clause 1 table applies only to the parts above it.
-- Because each table is a sum of bands, the tax on the parts from w to x is the table tax up to x less the table tax up to w.
GIVEN `p` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the tax under Schedule 7` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the item 1 rate in percent` (`p`'s `year of income begins`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `r` THEN
        JUST (
                `p`'s `superannuation remainder` TIMES 45 DIVIDED BY 100
            PLUS `p`'s `employment termination remainder` TIMES 45 DIVIDED BY 100
            PLUS `the working holiday table tax up to` (`p`'s `working holiday taxable income`)
            PLUS `the table tax on the parts above working holiday income` `p` `r`
        )

GIVEN `p` IS AN Individual, `r` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the table tax on the parts above working holiday income` MEANS
    IF `a resident taxpayer` `p`
    THEN     `the resident table tax up to` (`the threshold that applies` `p`) `r` (`the ordinary taxable income` `p`)
       MINUS `the resident table tax up to` (`the threshold that applies` `p`) `r` (`p`'s `working holiday taxable income`)
    ELSE     `the non-resident table tax up to` (`the ordinary taxable income` `p`)
       MINUS `the non-resident table tax up to` (`p`'s `working holiday taxable income`)

§§ `s 23AA -- base rate entity`

-- "An entity is a base rate entity for a year of income if: (a) no more than 80% of its assessable income for the year of
-- income is base rate entity passive income; and (b) its aggregated turnover (within the meaning of the Income Tax Assessment
-- Act 1997) for the year of income, worked out as at the end of that year, is less than $50 million."
DECLARE Company HAS
    `assessable income` IS A NUMBER
    `base rate entity passive income` IS A NUMBER
    `aggregated turnover` IS A NUMBER
    `taxable income` IS A NUMBER
    `a non-profit company` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `c` IS A Company
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a base rate entity` MEANS
        `c`'s `base rate entity passive income` AT MOST `c`'s `assessable income` TIMES 80 DIVIDED BY 100
    AND `c`'s `aggregated turnover` LESS THAN 50000000

§§ `s 23(2) -- the company rate`

-- "The rate of tax in respect of the taxable income of a company is: (a) if the company is a base rate entity for a year of
-- income -- 25%; or (b) otherwise -- 30%; if subsections (3) to (5) and section 23A do not apply to the company."
GIVEN `c` IS A Company
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the company rate in percent` MEANS IF `a base rate entity` `c` THEN 25 ELSE 30

§§ `s 23(6) -- non-profit companies`

-- "The amount of tax payable by a company (before applying any ... tax offset ...) must not be greater than 55% of the amount
-- (if any) by which the taxable income of the company exceeds $416, if: (a) the company is a non-profit company; and (b) the
-- taxable income is not greater than: (i) if the company is a base rate entity for a year of income -- $762; or (ii) otherwise --
-- $915."
GIVEN `c` IS A Company
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the non-profit ceiling` MEANS `the slice` (`c`'s `taxable income`) 416 `no upper limit` TIMES 55 DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN `c` IS A Company
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the non-profit ceiling applies` MEANS
        `c`'s `a non-profit company`
    AND (    (`a base rate entity` `c` AND `c`'s `taxable income` AT MOST 762)
          OR ((NOT `a base rate entity` `c`) AND `c`'s `taxable income` AT MOST 915))

GIVEN `c` IS A Company
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the company tax before offsets` MEANS
    IF `c`'s `taxable income` AT MOST 0 THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the non-profit ceiling applies` `c`
        THEN `the lesser of` (`c`'s `taxable income` TIMES `the company rate in percent` `c` DIVIDED BY 100) (`the non-profit ceiling` `c`)
        ELSE `c`'s `taxable income` TIMES `the company rate in percent` `c` DIVIDED BY 100
